---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — FeeCalc"
  description="How FeeCalc handles your data: it doesn't. Calculations run locally in your browser."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Your numbers stay in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Everything you type into the calculator — amounts, currencies, fee rates — is processed
      locally on your device. Nothing is sent to a server, stored in a database, or shared with
      anyone. There is no backend involved in the calculation.
    </p>
    <h2>No tracking, no accounts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics, tracking scripts, session replay or fingerprinting.</li>
      <li>No advertising or third-party ad scripts.</li>
      <li>No accounts, logins, cookies for tracking, or personal data collection.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Shared links</h2>
    <p>
      The "copy link" button puts your current inputs into the page URL (for example
      <code>?amt=1000&amp;cur=USD</code>) so you can share a configured calculation. If you share
      that URL, whoever opens it sees those inputs — don't put anything sensitive in it. A plain
      link to this site contains nothing about you.
    </p>
    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      Like any website, our hosting provider may keep standard request logs (IP address, browser,
      page requested) for security and operations. We don't use them to profile visitors.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
